messages:
zoe_cs: LatticeAI POC stuck during onboarding. They see auth 401s then a cascade of 429s once their workers retry. They mentioned envoy + a managed gateway that inserts a large tracing cookie.
zoe_cs: Mica from Lattice pasted: 'gateway adds trace=eyJz... (~410b). Combined with our Bearer token it sometimes gets mangled.'
pat_eng: That sounds like header-size or truncation at the gateway. If Authorization is altered we return 401 on the handshake. Retries without jitter cause fanout -> 429s on our rate limiter.
ravi_sre: Also observed many short-lived TLS sessions from their serverless pool -> cold-start fanout.
anya_support: They're on go-sdk v0.3.1. Any quick mitigation we can recommend to unblock the POC?
pat_eng: Short-term: 1) ask gateway to stop injecting the tracing cookie for /v1/auth (route-level strip). 2) move tracing payload to a POST body to internal telemetry instead of a cookie. 3) patch client to use jittered backoff on first auth attempts.
mica_lattice: We can change gateway rules. How quick is the client patch?
pat_eng: Tiny wrapper example (Go pseudo):
```
// go pseudo
func AuthWithBackoff(authFunc func() error) error {
  for i:=0;i<5;i++ {
    if err:=authFunc(); err==nil { return nil }
    time.Sleep(time.Duration((1<<i)*100 + rand.Intn(100)) * time.Millisecond)
  }
  return fmt.Errorf("auth failed")
}
```
ravi_sre: Ops action: add onboarding checklist entry "check gateway cookie/tracing size" and emit a first-call metric for Authorization length > 300 bytes.
devex_bot: Added ticket: docs/onboarding/gateway-tracing-cookie.md and infra/telemetry/auth-header-length-alert :white_check_mark:
mica_lattice: We applied route-level strip and changed tracing to POST. After the client patch and short-term splay, 401s disappeared and the 429 bursts stopped. POC progressing.
zoe_cs: Great. I'll update their renewal risk to green and include the playbook steps in the handoff. Thanks team. :raised_hands:
